flowchart TD
  A[Frontend or caller invokes identify and load] --> B[rc_client_begin_identify_and_load_game]
  B --> C[Hash source media or supplied data]
  C --> D[rc_client_load_game]
  D --> E[Local client hash record]
  E --> F{Known game ID?}
  F -->|No| G[Resolve hash through configured server callback]
  F -->|Yes| H[Fetch game sets through configured server callback]
  G --> H
  H --> I[Parse and prepare game subsets]
  I --> J[Start session through configured server callback]
  J --> K[rc_client_activate_game]
  K --> L[Validate requested asset addresses through read-memory callback]
  L --> M[Activate runtime assets]
  M --> N[rc_client_do_frame]
  N --> O[Update runtime memrefs through configured read-memory callback]
  O --> P[Evaluate active achievements leaderboards and Rich Presence]
  P --> Q[Raise pending events]
  Q --> R[Award or leaderboard request through configured server callback]

  M --> S[Explicit media change only]
  S --> T[rc_client_begin_identify_and_change_media]
  T --> U[Hash unless cached path record is reused]
  U --> V[Resolve changed-media hash when required]
  V --> W[Change media internal]

  M --> X[Reset]
  X --> Y[Check existing client game-hash record then reset runtime]
  M --> Z[Progress deserialization]
  Z --> AA[Deserialize runtime progress; no hash call in reviewed path]
  M --> AB[Unload]
  AB --> AC[Detach game and cancel game-related scheduled work]

  classDef boundary fill:#fff2cc,stroke:#a67c00,color:#000;
  class G,H,J,R,V boundary;
